{"html":"<p>Almost every Java backend reads and writes a database. There are two levels to know: <strong>JDBC</strong>, the low-level API where you write SQL yourself, and <strong>JPA</strong>, which maps rows to Java objects for you. Spring Data JPA sits on top and writes most queries for you. Each level hides the one below, but you need to understand it when things go wrong.</p>\n<h2 id=\"jdbc-sql-from-java\">JDBC: SQL From Java</h2>\n<p>JDBC is part of the JDK. You open a connection, send SQL, and read the results row by row. This example uses H2, a small in-memory database:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> url</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"jdbc:h2:mem:shop\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Connection</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> conn</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> DriverManager.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getConnection</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(url, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"sa\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> insert</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"INSERT INTO book (title, pages) VALUES (?, ?)\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (PreparedStatement</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> ps</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> conn.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">prepareStatement</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(insert)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        ps.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setString</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Dune\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        ps.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setInt</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">412</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        ps.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">executeUpdate</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> query</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"SELECT id, title, pages FROM book WHERE pages > ? ORDER BY title\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (PreparedStatement</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> ps</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> conn.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">prepareStatement</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(query)) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        ps.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setInt</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">400</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">        try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (ResultSet</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> rs</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> ps.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">executeQuery</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">            while</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (rs.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">next</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">                books.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">add</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(rs.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getLong</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"id\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), rs.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getString</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"title\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">), rs.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getInt</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"pages\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">            }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Three things to notice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>try-with-resources</strong> closes the connection, statement and result set, even on errors. Leaked connections are a classic production outage.</li>\n<li><code>rs.next()</code> moves to the next row, and the getters read columns by name.</li>\n<li>The <code>?</code> placeholders are filled with <code>setString</code>, <code>setInt</code> and so on.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"always-use-preparedstatement\">Always Use PreparedStatement</h3>\n<p>Never build SQL by gluing user input into a string:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// DANGEROUS: title = \"x' OR '1'='1\" returns every row</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> sql</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"SELECT * FROM book WHERE title = '\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> title </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"'\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>That&#39;s <strong>SQL injection</strong>, one of the most common security holes. With a <code>PreparedStatement</code>, the value is sent separately from the SQL, so <code>x&#39; OR &#39;1&#39;=&#39;1</code> is just a title that matches nothing.</p>\n<h3 id=\"transactions\">Transactions</h3>\n<p>By default, each statement is committed on its own. To make several changes all-or-nothing, turn off auto-commit, then commit or roll back:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">conn.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setAutoCommit</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">false</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">try</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    debit.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">executeUpdate</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    credit.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">executeUpdate</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    conn.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">commit</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">} </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">catch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (SQLException </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">e</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    conn.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">rollback</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    throw</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> e;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>In real apps, connections come from a <strong>pool</strong> (HikariCP is Spring Boot&#39;s default), because opening a new connection for every request is slow.</p>\n<h2 id=\"jpa-objects-instead-of-rows\">JPA: Objects Instead of Rows</h2>\n<p>Writing <code>rs.getString(…)</code> for every column gets old fast. <strong>JPA</strong> (Jakarta Persistence) is a standard for mapping classes to tables; <strong>Hibernate</strong> is the most used implementation. You describe the mapping with annotations:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Entity</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">GeneratedValue</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Long</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> id;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> title;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> author;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> int</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> pages;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    protected</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {}   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// JPA needs a no-argument constructor</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">title</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">author</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> pages</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) { … }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Hibernate now generates the SQL to insert, load, update and delete <code>Book</code> objects.</p>\n<h2 id=\"spring-data-jpa-repositories\">Spring Data JPA: Repositories</h2>\n<p>With Spring Data, you don&#39;t even write the data access class. Declare an interface:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> interface</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> BookRepository</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> JpaRepository</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Long</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    List&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findByAuthorIgnoreCase</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">author</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    Optional&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findFirstByTitle</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(String </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">title</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    List&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findByPagesGreaterThanOrderByTitleAsc</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> pages</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Query</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"select b from Book b where b.pages between :min and :max\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    List&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> </span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findWithPagesBetween</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">int</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><ul>\n<li><code>JpaRepository</code> already gives you <code>save</code>, <code>findById</code>, <code>findAll</code>, <code>deleteById</code>, paging and more.</li>\n<li><strong>Derived queries</strong> are built from the method name: <code>findByPagesGreaterThanOrderByTitleAsc(400)</code> becomes <code>WHERE pages &gt; ? ORDER BY title ASC</code>.</li>\n<li><code>@Query</code> takes a <strong>JPQL</strong> query, which looks like SQL but uses class and field names, for anything the name can&#39;t express.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"changes-are-saved-automatically\">Changes Are Saved Automatically</h3>\n<p>Inside a transaction, JPA keeps track of the entities it loaded. Change one, and Hibernate writes the update when the transaction commits, without calling <code>save</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Transactional</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">public</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> renameBook</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(Long id, String title) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    Book</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> book</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> repository.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findById</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(id).</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">orElseThrow</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    book.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">rename</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(title);   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// UPDATE happens at commit</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>This is called <strong>dirty checking</strong>. It&#39;s convenient, but it surprises people who expect nothing to happen without <code>save</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-n-1-problem\">The N+1 Problem</h2>\n<p>The most famous JPA performance trap. Say each <code>Author</code> has a list of books, loaded <strong>lazily</strong> (only when accessed):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">List</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Author</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">> </span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">authors</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> authorRepository.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">findAll</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();   </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 1 query</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (Author</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> author</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> :</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> authors) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    author.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">getBooks</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">().</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">size</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();                       </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 1 query per author!</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>With 100 authors, that&#39;s 101 queries. Fix it by loading what you need in one query:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">@</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">Query</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"select a from Author a left join fetch a.books\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">List</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Author</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> findAllWithBooks</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Or use <code>@EntityGraph(attributePaths = &quot;books&quot;)</code> on the repository method. Turn on SQL logging in development (<code>spring.jpa.show-sql=true</code>) so you see how many queries a page really runs.</p>\n<h2 id=\"which-level-when\">Which Level When?</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Situation</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Typical CRUD in a Spring app</td>\n<td>Spring Data JPA repositories</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A complex report, or a query JPA makes awkward</td>\n<td><code>@Query</code> with native SQL, or JdbcTemplate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bulk inserts of millions of rows</td>\n<td>JDBC batch updates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Learning what&#39;s really happening</td>\n<td>JDBC, once</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>JDBC sends SQL from Java; always close resources with try-with-resources.</li>\n<li>Always use <code>PreparedStatement</code> with <code>?</code> placeholders: it prevents SQL injection.</li>\n<li>JPA maps classes to tables with <code>@Entity</code> and <code>@Id</code>; Hibernate writes the SQL.</li>\n<li>Spring Data repositories give CRUD for free, derive queries from method names, and take JPQL with <code>@Query</code>.</li>\n<li>Watch for N+1 queries on lazy relations, and fix them with <code>join fetch</code> or an entity graph.</li>\n</ol>\n"}